  m_Name: L15_Efes
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Cutrium.Presentation::Cutrium.Presentation.Landmark.LandmarkDefinition
  _landmarkId: efes-antik-kenti
  _displayTitle: Ancient City of Ephesus
  _shortDescription: Ephesus was one of the largest port and trading cities of the
    Roman era. The Library of Celsus, marble streets, and Great Theatre still convey
    its splendour. The nearby Temple of Artemis was counted among the Seven Wonders
    of the Ancient World, while mosaics and frescoes in the terrace houses offer
    a close view of wealthy urban life.
  _sector: Izmir / TURKEY
  _displayTitleTurkish: Efes Antik Kenti
  _shortDescriptionTurkish: "Efes, Roma d\xF6neminin en b\xFCy\xFCk liman ve ticaret
    kentlerinden biriydi. Celsus K\xFCt\xFCphanesi, mermer caddeleri ve B\xFCy\xFCk
    Tiyatrosu kentin g\xF6rkemini bug\xFCn h\xE2l\xE2 g\xFC\xE7l\xFC bi\xE7imde hissettirir.
    Yak\u0131ndaki Artemis Tap\u0131na\u011F\u0131 Antik D\xFCnyan\u0131n Yedi Harikas\u0131
    aras\u0131nda say\u0131l\u0131rken, teras evlerdeki mozaik ve freskler zengin
    kentlilerin g\xFCnl\xFCk ya\u015Fam\u0131na yak\u0131ndan bakmay\u0131 sa\u011Flar."
  _sectorTurkish: "\u0130zmir / T\xDCRK\u0130YE"
